/*!
@addtogroup usbd_ehci_cmsis_driver
@details This section describes the programming interface of the USB Device EHCI Cortex Microcontroller
 Software Interface Standard (CMSIS) driver. This driver defines generic peripheral driver interfaces
 for middleware making it reusable across a wide range of supported microcontroller devices. The API
 connects microcontroller peripherals with middleware that implements communication stacks, file
 systems, or other USB device class implementations.
 More information and usage method see http://www.keil.com/pack/doc/cmsis/Driver/html/index.html.

The driver implements the ARM_DRIVER_USBD interface and exposes Driver_USBD1 for use by CMSIS
USB Device middleware or validation frameworks. It wraps the MCUXpresso SDK USB Device EHCI
stack and handles clock configuration, endpoint management, and interrupt routing.

# Typical use case {#USBDTpyUC}

~~~~~{.c}
    /* Obtain pointer to the CMSIS USB Device driver */
    extern ARM_DRIVER_USBD Driver_USBD1;
    ARM_DRIVER_USBD *usbd = &Driver_USBD1;

    /* Register device and endpoint event callbacks */
    usbd->Initialize(DeviceEvent_Callback, EndpointEvent_Callback);

    /* Power on the USB Device controller */
    usbd->PowerControl(ARM_POWER_FULL);

    /* Connect to the USB bus */
    usbd->DeviceConnect();

    /* Handle device events in the application loop */
    while (1)
    {
        /* Application processes DeviceEvent_Callback and EndpointEvent_Callback
           notifications to respond to enumeration, endpoint transfers, etc. */
    }
~~~~~

*/
